      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "`more_itertools.chunked` keeps the leftover items and returns them as a final, shorter chunk. It doesn't pad or drop them.\n\n```python\nfrom more_itertools import chunked\nlist(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], 3))\n# [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7]]\n```\n\nRelated options:\n- **`strict=True`** (added in more-itertools 8.9) raises `ValueError` if the iterable can't be split into equal chunks. It only takes effect when you also pass `n`.\n- **`grouper`** is the one to use if you want the last chunk padded with a fill value. It takes `fillvalue`, and its `incomplete` argument can also be set to `'ignore'` to drop the leftovers or `'strict'` to raise.\n- **`chunked_even`** spreads the items so the chunk sizes are as even as possible.",
